      "message": "rest: don't log an error for /spenttxouts on a block without undo data\n\n`/rest/spenttxouts/<hash>` calls `ReadBlockUndo()` for every block above\ngenesis. For a block that was stored but never connected (a side branch)\nor whose undo data was pruned, `GetUndoPos()` is null, so\n`OpenUndoFile()` fails and `ReadBlockUndo()` writes \"OpenUndoFile failed\nfor FlatFilePos(nFile=-1, nPos=0)\" to debug.log with `LogError`. The\nendpoint then correctly answers 404, but every unauthenticated request\nfor such a block adds an `[error]` line that looks like disk corruption.\n\nCheck `CheckBlockDataAvailability()` for `BLOCK_HAVE_UNDO` first and\nonly read the undo file when it can exist. Pruning clears\n`BLOCK_HAVE_UNDO`, so this covers pruned blocks too. The response is\nunchanged.\n\nThe new interface_rest.py check requests a side-branch block and fails\non master because of the logged error.",
